# Database & TypeORM Rules

## Convenciones de Naming

- **Propiedades TypeScript**: camelCase en inglés (`productId`, `minimumStock`)
- **Columnas DB**: snake_case en inglés (`product_id`, `minimum_stock`)
- **Tablas**: plural en inglés (`products`, `movements`)

## Entidades TypeORM

```typescript
@Entity('products')
export class Product {
  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn()
  id: number;

  @Column({ unique: true, length: 50 })
  sku: string;

  @Column({ length: 200 })
  name: string;

  @Column({ type: 'decimal', precision: 10, scale: 2 })
  price: number;

  @Column({ name: 'minimum_stock', default: 0 })
  minimumStock: number;

  @Column({ type: 'enum', enum: ProductStatus, default: ProductStatus.ACTIVE })
  status: ProductStatus;

  @CreateDateColumn({ name: 'created_at' })
  createdAt: Date;
}
```

## Reglas de Stock

El stock se calcula dinámicamente; **no crear columna `stock`** en `products`.

```typescript
async calculateStock(productId: number): Promise<number> {
  const result = await this.movementRepository
    .createQueryBuilder('movement')
    .select(`SUM(CASE WHEN movement.type = 'inbound' THEN movement.quantity ELSE 0 END)`, 'inboundTotal')
    .addSelect(`SUM(CASE WHEN movement.type = 'outbound' THEN movement.quantity ELSE 0 END)`, 'outboundTotal')
    .where('movement.product_id = :productId', { productId })
    .getRawOne();

  return Number(result.inboundTotal) - Number(result.outboundTotal);
}
```
